@!internal
--[[
Non-suspending teardown for native GPU context state.

This helper releases the native device context used by
[](nupp.runtime.provider.nativegpu). It marks the state closed and clears its
handle before releasing the device through [](nupp.runtime.provider.gpudevice),
making repeated cleanup a no-op. It implements the provider's destruction
callback behind the canonical [](nupp.gpu.api) cleanup identity; it is not a
separately selectable service.

The callback accepts only state created by the native GPU implementation and
must not be used with browser contexts or arbitrary public context values.
]]
module nupp.runtime.provider.nativegpurelease

local device = require("nupp.runtime.provider.gpudevice")
export function destroy(state: any): nil
    if state._closed then
        return
    end
    state._closed = true
    local handle = state._handle
    state._handle = nil
    -- Closing settles nothing that can suspend: it only waits on the device.
    local close = device.close as @nosuspend function(any): (any, string?)
    close(handle)
end
